      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14264040/assets/08d900690b841d132b3451ca7f8e5013ee1e9a5383c541c926f9e921639d0e5f.png)\n\nLet $C(0,2)$ and $D(4,-1).$ Find $|\\overset{\\to }{CD}|.$",
      "worked_solution": "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OC}=c=0i+2j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OD}=d=4i-j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{CD}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CD} & =\\overset{\\to }{OD}-\\overset{\\to }{OC} \\\\  & =d-c \\\\  & =(4i-j)-(2j) \\\\  & =4i-3j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{CD}| & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
